Z||000006||88formula||08-13-2000||01:22 PM||||I don't think anyone has ever tried nitrous on an iron duke so how do these guys really know how well it will hold up? I know that a turbo has been installed on a duke in the past with success that I think made 150 hp. I would try it only if you can afford to loose the motor. I'm not trying to be sarcastic but you never know.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000007||theogre||08-13-2000||01:41 PM||||At the very least I'd replace all the head bolts before trying it. If you replace the bolts one at a time you won't need to remove the head. You will need a valve cover gasket set but that's cheap.<P>I wouln't try this at all on an 84 unless your sure the rods are the good ones. 84's had allot of problems with a batch of bad rods.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Pontiaddict||08-13-2000||01:53 PM||||I woudn't have thought a Civic would take nitrous either. You never know what will happen until you try.<P>Just make sure the duke is in good runing order. If it's spark knockng or burning oil, then don't try it. <P>If you're that concerned about popping a motor, then take the decklid off so you don't put the motor through it.||||reg||1
